---
import SitePage from '../layouts/SitePage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<SitePage title="Contact — Mortal Shell 2 Wiki" heading="Contact the editorial team" description="Send a specific guide correction, privacy question or rights request to the Mortal Shell 2 Wiki operator through the site email contact.">

<section><h2>Email contact</h2>
<p>Contact the operator of {SITE.name} at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. This is the site's editorial contact. We do not offer a live support desk, guarantee a response time, or handle game purchases, refunds or account recovery.</p>
<p>Unofficial fan guide. Not affiliated with Cold Symmetry or Playstack. For a game account or storefront problem, use the support channel linked by the relevant developer, publisher or store. Do not send us a password, security code, payment detail or private account token.</p></section>
<section><h2>Reporting an inaccurate guide</h2>
<p>Include the page URL, the heading or sentence at issue, and what you think is wrong. Where relevant, include the platform, game version and date of your observation. A link to a published patch note or a short description of repeatable steps helps distinguish a changed mechanic from a one-off player report.</p>
<p>A useful subject line is “Guide correction — [page title]”. If the issue involves a claimed fix, describe what happened before and after the suggested action. Please crop screenshots to the relevant game interface and remove names, messages or other private information. We do not need an entire save folder to consider a wording correction.</p></section>
<section><h2>Rights and content-removal requests</h2>
<p>Identify the affected page and the specific text or image, describe your relationship to the rights involved, and explain the requested action. A direct link to the original work or other relevant information can help us locate the issue. You do not need to send government identity documents in an initial request.</p>
<p>We review the material and may ask for clarification before making a change. The site does not own the game's artwork or trademarks. If material needs to be removed or corrected, the request can concern that material without requiring deletion of every unrelated guide on the same subject.</p></section>
<section><h2>Privacy and follow-up</h2>
<p>Email includes your address and anything you choose to send. Use the subject “Privacy request” if you want to ask about a previous message or request its deletion. Include enough context to locate the correspondence without adding unnecessary personal information. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains the limits of our control over mailbox and hosting-provider records.</p>
<p>There is no on-site contact form, public comment system or file-upload service. Our <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a> explains how a correction can affect an article's wording and update date.</p></section>
</SitePage>
